melody:
# Chorus as published in 1924 (cut time, written here with quarter-note beats; "I'll" is the pickup)
I'll see you in my dreams,
E4(2) D4(2) F4(2) G4(2) A4(2) G4(4) ~G4(4)
hold you in my dreams,
A4(2) C5(2) D5(2) E5(2) D5(4) ~D5(4)
some-one took you out of my arms,
D5(2) D4(2) E4(2) F#4(2) C5 A4 C5 A4 ~A4(4)
still I feel the thrill of your charms;
A4(2) D4(2) E4(2) F4(2) A4 G4 A4 G4 ~G4(4)
lips that once were mine,
D4(2) F4(2) G4(2) A4(2) G4(4) ~G4(4)
ten-der eyes that shine,
A4(2) C5(2) D5(2) E5(2) D5(4) ~D5(4)
they will light my way to-night,
Eb5(2) D5(2) C5(3) D4 A4(2) G4(2) F4(3)
I'll see you in my dreams.
E4 D4(2) F4(2) G4(2) A4(2) F4(4) ~F4 r r

# Once more
I'll see you in my dreams,
E4 D4(2) F4(2) G4(2) A4(2) G4(4) ~G4(4)
hold you in my dreams,
A4(2) C5(2) D5(2) E5(2) D5(4) ~D5(4)
some-one took you out of my arms,
D5(2) D4(2) E4(2) F#4(2) C5 A4 C5 A4 ~A4(4)
still I feel the thrill of your charms;
A4(2) D4(2) E4(2) F4(2) A4 G4 A4 G4 ~G4(4)
lips that once were mine,
D4(2) F4(2) G4(2) A4(2) G4(4) ~G4(4)
ten-der eyes that shine,
A4(2) C5(2) D5(2) E5(2) D5(4) ~D5(4)
they will light my way to-night,
Eb5(2) D5(2) C5(3) D4 A4(2) G4(2) F4(3)
I'll see you in my dreams.
E4 D4(2) F4(2) G4(2) A4(2) F4(4) ~F4 r r(2)
